Focl uses a custom license, the terms of which are as follows:

Focl permits programs to embed or use Focl as part of their projects, regardless of whether they are open-source or proprietary, and allows both static and dynamic linking.

There is only one circumstance under which users are required to open-source part of their code:

When users modify Focl's code (including its built-in commands and core libraries) and publish their program with modified Focl embeded, they must make the modified portions publicly available with this License. Note that user-defined commands or additional components are not subject to this requirement.

The portion concerning the built-in library linenoise is not covered under the terms of this license. Please refer to its own BSD-2-Clause license at https://github.com/antirez/linenoise/LICENSE.

Disclaimer of Warranty:

    "This software is provided 'as is', without any express or implied warranties, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose. The author shall not be liable for any direct or indirect damages."

Definition of "Open-Sourcing Modified Portions":

    "'Open-sourcing the modified portions' means that such portions shall be made publicly available in source code form through a public code hosting platform (e.g., GitHub, Gitee, etc.) and provided to third parties under the same terms as this license."